{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795282684,"nonce":"G6lJ0/06DIwOPGVGVgLTOEOQDXM=","title":"One Rust server serves the game over HTTPS and holds the rooms of the bus","message":"**Outcome.** The crate server serves web/ over HTTPS on port 5201, with a self-signed certificate that it keeps until the addresses of the machine change. Its bus at /ws holds rooms as design.md describes them under Rooms. GET /rooms lists the rooms. The server never reads a binary message. A load subcommand measures the delay of the bus.\n\n**Requirements.** N1, N2, N3, N7, N8, N9, E2, E4.\n\n**Done when.** Tests drive the rooms over streams in memory, with no TLS and no HTTP: join, create, the three refusals, the limits, the status frame, the control frames of the owner, and the removal of an empty room. The load test reports the delay for 16 clients.\n\nBelongs to the plan, issue 1d9449d.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}